
  TOURNAMENT-LATTICE PROPAGATION: THM D, H-GAPS, Cl2(pi/3)
======================================================================

  PART 1 [VERIFIED] Theorem D: loose gaps of V* lie on the (2n-1) lattice
    n Q=2n-1  #lonely intervals    centers * Q (near integers)
   10     19                  2                  [6.99, 12.01]
   12     23                  2                  [7.01, 15.99]
   16     31                  2                 [10.99, 20.01]
   18     35                  2                 [11.01, 23.99]
   22     43                  2                 [14.99, 28.01]
  => the only V* gaps are {3,2n-4} pinches (on the (2n-1) lattice). [Theorem D content]

  PART 2 [VERIFIED/REFUTED] H-impossibilities
  H(T)=#HamPaths is always odd. Forbidden odd values <=80: {7, 21}.
  Tempting pattern 7*3^k={7,21,63,189}: REFUTED -- 63,189 achievable (first at n=8).
  (n<=7 sampling missed 63; verified 63 hit 6x and 189 hit 121x at n=8.)
  So forbidden-H is sporadic {7,21}; the powers-of-3 live in the 3-shell, not here.

  PART 3 [NUMERICAL/STRUCTURAL] the 1.014 constant
  Cl_2(pi/3) = 1.014942  (tournament tropical constant numerator, HYP-707)
  unit-distance disproof exponent: > 1.014 (Sawin, a LOWER bound, no closed form)
  => 'UD exponent = Cl_2(pi/3)' UNVERIFIED; shared object is the prime-3 angle pi/3
     (Eisenstein zeta_6): triangular UD lattice Cay(Z[zeta_6]) AND the tropical log-sin sum.

